	I have found this business of downloading the fonts to be
pretty tricky. For one thing, you have to make sure that the permission
on all the font files is 444. You may alos have to have world read
permission on the entire path but I have not been able to verify that.
The contents of the font.paths file have to have the correct path also.
So, to download the font paths, you would say something like:

	your.ip.address.here:/tftpboot/vt1000/font.paths

Be sure that the tftpd is enables in /etc.inetd.conf

The font.paths file should contain a list of paths to all the fonts,
something like -

	./100dpi/avant_garde...

If you use a relative path, make sure it will work, otherwise use the
full path name.

If you are only using 100dpi fonts, then edit the 75dpi paths out of
font.paths, to speed up loading (which can take forever if you have
lots of fonts).
