From hoyt@bessie.ENET.DEC.COM Mon Apr 16 15:55:59 1990

Step 1. vi /etc/inetd.conf and make the following changes 
	
	a. remove the # in fromt of the line for tftp

	b. edit the line for tftp to read 
 tftp    dgram   udp     wait    /usr/etc/tftpd tftpd -r  
/usr/lib/X11/fonts/decwin  

	c. remove the # in front of the line bootp 

	d. the line should look like the one below

	 bootp   dgram   udp     wait    /usr/etc/bootpd     bootpd -i

Step 2. Next create  or edit the file /usr/etc/bootptab

	add the following line 

vt1000 1 08:00:2b:12:d6:bf 16.72.0.38 /usr/lib/X11/fonts/decwin/font.paths

Step 3. Next you need to create the file font.paths

	a.  cd /usr/lib/X11/fonts/decwin
	
	b. type in one of the following comands depending on version
	   of uws.
	 
	  1. for uws v2.1 
		a. cd /usr/lib/dwf

		b. find 75dpi 100dpi -name ".dwf" -print > font.paths

	  2. for uws 2.2

		a. cd /usr/lib/X11/fonts/decwin

		b. find 75dpi 100dpi -name ".pcf" -print > font.paths

	NOTE make sure that your font path file is world read

Step 4.

	Kill off the inetd process and restart it this will
	make it use the changes in inetd.conf.


	
Step 5.  On the vt1000 seclect the font path... under the pull down
	from customize menu.

	Now select tftp font path
	next edit the line tftp font path ROM,
	to read ROM,xx.xx.xx.xx:font.paths (were xx.xx.xx.xx is hosts
						tcp/ip address)
	next select apply

	You will get a message box on the screen it will tell you
	it loading the fonts and that this will take about 7 mins.
	the pointer will turn to the clock style. After about 11 mins
	on mkunix the vt1000 will come back and tell you that the
	font path was set and the number of fonts in the path.

This is what we did here.


