				 Announce

		       Their SPRING 1990 Conference

			      To Be Held At
		The University Centre, Mill Lane, Cambridge, UK
				   On
			    Friday 4th May 1990

		             10:30 am - 4:30 pm

	---------------------------------------------------------

The Conference Theme will be X User Interfaces, their origins and development.

The conference programme is for a full day and will consist of eight technical
sessions with presentations from major manufacturers as well as from end-users,
who will share the benefits of their experience. The proceedings will be opened
by the Chairman, Niall Mansfield, with an overview of X's likely future and
opportunities that this offers.

Throughout the day there will also be an exhibition of X Products and
services.  The Exhibition will be open from 09:00 - 17:00 and will also be
open to people not attending the conference itself.

Attendance at the conference will cost 50 pounds sterling for EXUG members,
and 75 pounds sterling for Non-members.  Advanced registration (prefered but
not essential) and membership requests should be sent to the EXUG secretary
at 185 High Street, Cottenham, Cambridgeshire, CB4 4RX, UK.  Email enquiries
can be sent to exug@unipalm.co.uk (aka exug@unipalm.uucp).

A few stands are still available, details can be obtained from the secretary.
Membership costs 25 pounds sterling for individual membership, 100 pounds
sterling for corporate memberships.  Benefits of EXUG membership include
Quarterly newsletter, discounts at EXUG conferences, and access to the
EXUG electronic mail Q&A service.


