Dick Seymour actually posted his original message after he and I tried to
boot VMS 5.3-1 on a VS3200 connected via an MDB converter to a Unibus
backplane (on a 750!).

After Mark Pizzolato posted his very astute response, I copied the PUDRIVER
and TSDRIVER (I have an AVIV TS-11 emulation board on the Unibus also)
from VMS 5.1-1 (since Mark said the change was in 5.2)
into the SYS$SYSROOT:[SYS$LDR].  The 3200 successfully booted!  The RA-81's
connected to my UDA-50 performed just fine, and were happy to be on
a faster computer.  I have since prevailed upon DEC to promise me driver
source so I can modify the drivers to remove calls to load the "ALT"
mapping registers.  The VMS 5.x DEVICE SUPPORT manual actually explains
the use of the 18-bit versus 22-bit mapping registers.

However, all is not rosy.  The 5.1 TSDRIVER did not recognize my tape drive
as being on-line, even though it sensed the controller (as a TSV05!).
I am still working on this - probably a still older driver is required.
Since many cables and boards are moved each time I test, I have not had
time to check.

