We have (or rather had) the same problem here.  My solution was
to drop in 4.3 init with the sunos 4.x code to demand the root
pw if "secure" is set in /etc/ttys (ttytab for sunos)

Here's what our ttys looks like:

  :0 "/usr/bin/login -P /usr/bin/Xprompter -C /usr/bin/dxsession" none on
window=/usr/bin/Xcfb"

Or if the console is in a "secure" location:

  :0 "/usr/bin/login -P /usr/bin/Xprompter -C /usr/bin/dxsession" none on
secure window=/usr/bin/Xcfb" 

Now replacing an init that has unknown (to me) features isn't something
that I'd recommend, I'm willing to give out the binary with disclaimers
(ie be careful and make sure you know what you're doing.)

jdh

