Lines: 13
Posted: Sat Apr 28 18:02:09 1990

The SMP support is for multiple CPUs on a single machine, not for grouping
together CPUs on different machines.  The SMP implementation assumes one
kernel image, hence one machine.

The RPC mechanism supported in ULTRIX 4.0 is based on H-P's Apollo Division's
NCS.  There are mechanisms in there for allowing different parts of applications
to run on various CPUs on a network.  ("The Network *is* the System", as was
the DECUS theme a few years back before some company took it, changed it,
and then trademarked the slogan.)

By the way, ULTRIX questions are best addressed in comp.unix.ultrix.

Fred


