1) There do not currently seem to be any alternatives to buying memory from DEC.   DEC is keeping the XMI bus proprietary and none of the 3-rd party vendors
   have reverse engineered it yet.  They will probably do so as the 6000 series
   installations increase, as long as DEC keeps the 6000 series memory prices
   high enough to make competition worthwhile.

2) The memory is the same as used for the VAX 6000 series.

