In article <2816@teda.UUCP>, bob@teda.UUCP (Bob Armstrong) writes:
> 
>   I have a C program in which calls to fopen are failing.  The errno ends up
> set to EVMSERR, and the vaxc$errno is RMS$_CHN, which says that the $ASSIGN
> service failed.
> [... etc ...]

  Thanks to those who responded to this problem.

  As it turns out, there is a bug in the VAXCRTL access, fopen and open
functions.  If you try to access a file which via a search list logical,
CRTL leaves one open channel for each element in the search list which
fails to contain the file.  Obviously it has a problem in cleaning up
after itself.  If you only do a few of these then there is no problem,
but if you do enough then you will eventually run out of open channels.
After that you can't open anything.

  We have a relatively old C compiler, version 2.4, so this may be a problem
that has been fixed.

