You don't really need the monitor plugged in but _ALL_ other bits (keyboard
& mouse) must be there as the power up diagnostics fail if they are not.
So this means you need to take the cable that goes to the Monitor/Keyboard/Mouse

Then power the thing up, wait for it to do it's diagnostics (perhaps you'd
like to time it with monitor in place first) type b<return> & away you go.

(the above applies to Vaxstn3100 also, don't know about DECstn's I don't have
one of those but if there is anyone out there that would like to make a
donation to medical science ;-)

