After begging Digital to believe us that we had the paging problem, we were
loaned an additional 16 MEG of memory to "get by" until "later".  We just kept
getting told that "no one else has this problem, therefore you don't".  I guess
we're just "lucky" to be one of the first, now that I look back...

It took more than 2 months to get us two patches, neither of which fixed the
problem.  To test it, we had to build a new kernels, remove the memory, and
run for about 3 days until it locked up.

Usually, the system would not allow us to call doadump successfully, even
though we set all the boot params to allow manual intervention upon reset.
doadump would usually error exit, or fail to start, and when we booted the
system, no dump existed.

We did manage to get two dumps and sent them to Digital.  As far as I know,
they were never really analyzed.

Recently, I was called and told by Ultrix Engineering that the "right" patch 
is available.  Also, I was told that someone from customer support would call
me to make sure I would get the patch sent to me.  I have never been
called back about the patch...

I have mostly given up.  We finally locked up with the paging problem the other
day even with the extra 16 meg, but we ran for over a month without failing.
I have to assume this is "the way" with Digital.  If you have a serious system
problem, you can't get it fixed.  I have talked to my local sales group for
help, of course I called customer support about 150 times, I have spoken to
Mad Dog about it (I don't think he ever did anything about it), I have
requested help from Fred Avolio (Fred /dev/null-io)....

I have been "rumored-at" that the bug is not fixed in UWS 2.3, but all will be
fixed in Ultrix 4.0.  When I get 4.0, I'll post our findings...


--John Hagan.


