4-3 ULTRIX V4.0 FACT SHEET

Product Name:  ULTRIX V4.0

Overview:

ULTRIX V4.0 is a major new release of Digitals implementation of
the UNIX operating system and provides many new features to
support commercial computing.  Distributed computing features
have been added to increase performance by using either Symmetric
Multiprocessing (SMP) in a tightly-coupled homogeneous
environment, or Remote Procedure Call (RPC) technology in a
loosely-coupled heterogeneous environment.  POSIX and XPG3
Conformance make it easier to port industry standard
applications.  Centralized administration has been improved by
new distributed services.   Larger systems are supported with 512
megabytes of RAM and 96 disks providing up to 144 gigabytes of
storage.  Because SQL runtime libraries are included, developers
do not have to purchase an SQL runtime license to run database
applications on ULTRIX.  ULTRIX V4.0 will be submitted to the
National Computer Security Center for certification at the
C2-level.

Key Features in Version 4.0 include:

    o  Hardware Support Enhancements
       -  Symmetric Multiprocessing (SMP) provides greatly
          increased system performance by allowing several
          tightly-coupled CPUs to perform all functions at the
          same time with the same kernel, with a single copy of
          the operating system resident in memory
       -  Maximum number of disks increased from 32 to 96 per
          system (up to 144 gigabytes of storage)
       -  Software support for physical memory increased from 128
          megabytes to 512 megabytes
       -  Client support for the PrintServer 20, PrintServer 40,
          and the PrintServer 40 Plus is included with ULTRIX
          V4.0 so that customers do not need to purchase separate
          media kits
       -  Differences between RISC and VAX systems are minimized
          because both the RISC and VAX binaries are generated
          from a single source pool
       -  Support for many new systems, peripherals, and
          communications products (see below)

    o  Distributed Services
      -   Remote Procedure Call (RPC) portion of Hewlett-Packard/
          Apollo's Network Computing System (NCS), including the
          Network Interface Definition Language Compiler and the
          Location Broker.  This is the first step in the joint
          development effort with Hewlett-Packard/Apollo to
          extend the RPC portion of NCS.  Digital is working with
          Hewlett-Packard in a joint development effort to extend
          the RPC portion of NCS.  Both companies are working
          together to extend the RPC capability to support
          wide-area networks, large data processing applications,
          international languages, and additional network
          platforms and protocols such as X.25 and OSI.
       -  Project Athena's Kerberos Authentication Service
          prevents one system from impersonating a second system,
          jeopardizing system security
       -  Project Athena's Hesiod Name Service allows centralized
          administration of the password database and other
          system management databases in a distributed fashion
       -  Network Time Protocol (NTP) enables synchronization of
          all clocks in an Internet network

    o  ULTRIX/SQL feature in base operating system includes:
       -  ULTRIX/SQL runtime engine with mullet-server
          architecture, intelligent query optimizer, tunable
          buffer management, tunable lock manager, and recovery
       -  DECnet and TCP/IP remote access
       -  Interactive SQL terminal monitor
       -  Database Administrator tools
       -  Optimization tools
       -  Forms runtime library
       -  Full set of user and database administrator
          documentation, including on-line man pages
       -  Several other products will be offered as ULTRIX/SQL
          optional layered products such as:
             * Embedded SQL preprocessors for C, FORTRAN, and Ada
             * ULTRIX/SQL to Rdb/VMS SQL source translators for C
               and FORTRAN
             * Rdb/VMS SQL to ULTRIX/SQL source translators for C
               and FORTRAN
             * A VMS layered product for remote access to Rdb/VMS
               from ULTRIX/SQL
             * Third-party and Digital front-end tools

    o  Standards compliance and support
       -  Conforms to the base level specification of the X/Open
          Portability Guide, Issue 3 (XPG3).  (As stated in
          previous announcements, Digital intends to brand ULTRIX
          according to X/Open's branding program once that
          program is in place).
       -  Conforms to the IEEE POSIX 1003.1-1988 (ISO
          9945-1:1990) standard and FIPS 151-1. FIPS (Federal
          Information Processing Standard) 151-1, issued in March
          by the National Institute of Standards and Technology
          (NIST), is the U.S. government's standard based on
          POSIX.  Digital intends to demonstrate compliance
          through the NIST POSIX Conformance Test Suite, once
          that is available and stable.
       -  Increased compatibility between ULTRIX and AT&T System
          V Interface Definition (SVID) with addition of AWK
          (nawk) program and K (Korn) shell
       -  Supports the X/Open Transport Interface (XTI) library
          which is specified in the X/Open Portability Guide.
          Digital has begun to provide a transition path for
          those customers who want to migrate to Open Systems
          Interconnection (OSI) networks from other protocols.
       -  Includes a comprehensive set of library routines,
          commands, and utilities to support
          internationalization, based on Native Language System
          (NLS) in XPG3; base system includes language support
          databases for French, English, and German (complies
          with ISO 8859/1 and ISO 646)

    o  System Management Features
       -  Enhancements to Virtual Memory Subsystem, including
       	  configurable virtual address limits and memory
          allocation requirements
       -  Ability to configure buffer cache and tailor additional
       	  parameters for increased performance
       -  License Management Facility (LMF) to allow activation
          of software such as user capacity upgrades without
          installation of additional software
       -  Diskless Management Service (DMS) and the Remote
          Installation Service (RIS) allow a single system to
          service both RISC and VAX systems at the same time
       -  RIS server performs the boot request on the local
          Ethernet and uses NFS to access the RIS files on the
          full RIS server; facilitates remote installations
          across gateways and wide area networks

    o  C2 Security Environment:
       Security on ULTRIX V4.0 contains features intended to
       fulfill the Department of Defense Trusted Computer Systems
       Evaluation Criteria for C2.  Features include:
       -  Discretionary access controls
       -  Improved log in controls - including long passwords,
          password aging, and randomly-generated passwords
       -  Event auditing and audit trail analysis - to track each
          system call and monitor other security-relevant events;
          report-generating tool is also provided
       -  Security features are fully-configurable, allowing
          system administrator to establish level of security
       -  Will be submitted to National Computer Security Center
          (NCSC) for C2 rating

    o  Network Support Enhancements
       -  NFS enhancements
       -  X/OPEN Transport Interface (XTI) is a transport service
          library which provides a common program interface for
          IP and OSI network transports; provides easy migration
          of applications as networks evolve from TCP/IP to OSI
       -  Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP) agent reports
          network management information

Minimum memory requirements:  The minimum memory required is 6mb
on a VAX system, and 8mb on a RISC system.

Hardware:

    o ULTRIX V4.0 provides support for Symmetric Multiprocessing
      (SMP) on these multiprocessor configurations:  DECsystem
      5820, DECsystem 5830, DECsystem 5840, all multiprocessor
      VAX 6000 systems, and all multiprocessor VAX 8000 systems.

    o Peripherals and communications devices supported include:
      ESE20, TA90, TQ7OL, RZ56, RZ57, RX23, RZ24, RF31, DDT-32,
      DEBNI and the DEMEANOR.

Pricing and Availability:
    o ULTRIX V4.0 is priced from $2000 on a MicroVAX 3100 to
      $199,640 on a VAX 9000.  The product may be ordered now,
      with deliveries beginning in summer, 1990.

