4-3 DECNET-ULTRIX V4.0 FACT SHEET

Product Name:  DECnet-ULTRIX Version 4

Overview:

DECnet-ULTRIX software enables communication among different,
networked Digital ULTRIX-based systems that use the DNA Phase IV
protocols and with Digital or non-Digital systems that use the
Internet (TCP/IP-based) protocols. DECnet-ULTRIX allows customers
to integrate all their Digital systems, including ULTRIX/RISC,
into a DECnet network.  DECnet-ULTRIX provides a transparent,
total networking solution in a heterogeneous environment so that
ULTRIX/VAX, ULTRIX/RISC, VMS, MS-DOS, and RSX systems on a DECnet
network can work together easily.

Key Features:
  o  Provides the following capabilities:  task-to-task
     communications, network virtual  terminal, remote file
     transfer, mail, and network-wide resource sharing and
     management as defined by the DNA protocols.
  o  Includes DECnet-Internet Gateway, an integral part of the
     DECnet-ULTRIX software. This feature provides a user on
     either the DECnet network or the Internet network the
     ability to:
       - transfer files bidirectionally;
       - log on to both DECnet and Internet systems from either
         type of system;
       - exchange mail;
       - access files on both types of systems.
  o  Provides enhanced DECnet-ULTRIX installation procedure.
     Kernel rebuild is not required during
     DECnet-ULTRIX	installation.
  o  License Management Facility (LMF) support for ease of
     system management.
  o  Allows for communication to X.25 networks using the
     X25router 2000 and DECnet data link mapping.  The following
     features have been added:
       - NCP to support X.25 protocol entities (DTE,
         network,group, destination, line and circuit);
       - EVL to support X.25 events.

U.S. Pricing and Availability:
DECnet-ULTRIX Version 4 is available immediately.  License prices
vary depending on processor.

