4-3 DECSTATION 5000 MODEL 200

PRODUCT NAME:  DECstation 5000 Model 200

OVERVIEW:

The DECstation 5000 Model 200 workstation is the most powerful
member of Digital's RISC-based DECstation family and is the
industry's best balanced desktop workstation.  Available in four
different graphics configurations, the DECstation 5000 Model 200
workstation is designed for compute-intensive 2D and 3D graphics
applications. The new systems support the TURBOchannel open I/O
interconnect which can be used to connect with peripherals
supported by industry-standard buses such as VME and SCSI.

The DECstation 5000 Model 200 system supports major industry
graphics standards, including Graphics Kernel System (GKS) and
Programmer's Hierarchical Interactive Graphics System (PHIGS).

The new workstation also delivers a high performance
implementation of PEX, the industry standard that links the
PHIGS/PHIGS+ Extension to the X Window System(tm).  Digital's
implementation of PEX includes support in the microcode to drive
the hardware directly, unlike other vendors' implementations that
layer PEX on graphics libraries and consequently result in
significant performance degradation.  Support for these standards
means that applications programs developed for the open systems
environment can generate graphic output on different devices
without modification to the source code.

The DECstation 5000 Model 200 system also supports powerful,
industry-standard user interfaces such as the Open Software
Foundation's Motif(tm) and the X Window System(tm), in addition
to DECwindows, Digital's user interface based on the X Window
System (tm).  The DECstation 5000 Model 200 system is completely
binary code compatible with Digital's family of DECstation and
DECsystem RISC systems.

The DECstation 5000 Model 200 system offers accelerated 2D and 3D
vector and polygon performance, graphics hardware features to
support antialiased vectors, true color display, and simultaneous
double and Z buffering.  The expandable range of configurations
are ideally suited for such applications as design automation
(CAD/CAM), financial and quantitative analysis, CASE, molecular
modeling, medical imaging, visual simulation, laboratory data
acquisition, seismic interpretation, technical publishing,
graphic arts, and animation.

Key Features:
    o MIPS R3000 CPU and R3010 FPU and LSI Logic LR3220 Write
      Buffer chipsets, operating at 25MHz and providing 24 MIPS
      (Dhrystone V1.1) performance.
    o 8 to 120 Mbytes of Error Correction Code (ECC) system
      memory.
    o 128 Kbytes of total system cache; 64 Kbytes of data cache
      and 64 Kbytes of instruction cache.
    o ThinWire Ethernet connector and BNC port (expandable
      through TURBOchannel option slots to a total of three
      supported Ethernet ports.)
    o Small Computer Systems Interface (SCSI) controller provides
      up to 5 Mbytes per second of I/O bandwidth, and supports up
      to seven external SCSI devices.
    o Three TURBOchannel slots, which can access 93
      Mbytes-per-second burst transfer rates, for expansion and
      support of peripheral devices which connect to
      industry-standard VME or SCSI buses.
    o Two RS232 25-pin serial ports support printers, modems, and
      3D dial and button box devices.
    o One RS232 15-pin serial port for the keyboard and mouse or
      tablet.
    o FDDI capabilities can be added with the FDDI single-width
      option card, providing 100 Mbits/second transfer rate in a
      timed token-passing network.

Configurations:

DECstation 5000 Model 200CX:

The Model 200CX system is the entry-level graphics workstation in
the DECstation 5000 series.  It is ideally suited for CASE,
technical publishing, and applications that demand high CPU and
I/O system performance but do not need accelerated graphics.  The
CX graphics option is a single-width TURBOchannel card that
provides:
    o 8 Planes of color frame buffer offering 256 displayable
      colors/greyshades
    o 1024 x 864 display resolution
    o Support for the VR297 16-inch color Trinitron (tm) monitor,
      VR299 19-inch color monitor, and VR262 19-inch monochrome
      monitor (for greyscale graphics) operating at 60 Hz

U.S. List Price Configuration:
    o 8 Mbytes Error Correction Code Memory (120 Mbytes maximum
      capacity)
    o 8 Plane grazed frame buffer
    o 19-inch VR262 monochrome monitor
    o Diskless (Maximum disk capacity:  21 Gbytes)

U.S. List Price:  $14,995

DECstation 5000 Model 200PX:

The DECstation 5000 Model 200PX workstation delivers fast 2D
vectors, polygons, and raster graphics performance and is ideal
for applications such as Electrical Computer Aided Design (ECAD)
and Mechanical Computer Aided Design (MCAD).  The PX graphics
option is a single-width TURBOchannel card that provides:
    o 8 Planes of color frame buffer offering 256 displayable
      colors/greyshades, full screen double-buffering for
      animation
    o PixelStamp, a graphics rendering processor for accelerated
      2D vectors, polygons, and pixel drawing operations
    o 1280 x 1024 display resolution
    o Support for the VRT19 19-inch color Trinitron (tm) monitor
      operating at 66 Hz

U.S. List Price Configuration:
    o 8 Mbytes ECC memory (120 Mbytes maximum capacity)
    o 8 Plane accelerated 2D color frame buffer
    o 19-inch VRT19 Trintron (tm) color monitor
    o Diskless (Maximum disk capacity:  21 Gbytes)

U.S. List Price:  $21,500

DECstation 5000 Model 200PXG:

The DECstation 5000 Model 200PXG workstation offers
high-performance 3D modeling and imaging graphics and is ideal
for design automation (CAD/CAE/CAM), seismic interpretation,
molecular modeling, architectural design, and true-color imaging
applications.  The PXG graphics option is a dual-width
TURBOchannel card that provides:
    o 8 or 24 (16.7 million colors) planes of high-resolution
      graphics with full-page double buffering
    o PixelStamp rendering processor chipset
    o Intel (tm) i860 64-bit RISC microprocessor running at 33
      MHz and functioning as a graphics accelerator for
      performing fast 2D and 3D geometric transformations
    o Optional 24-bit Z buffer, available for applications
      demanding hardware-supported hidden surface removal
    o 1280 x 1024 display resolution
    o Support for the VRT19 19-inch color Trinitron (tm) monitor
      operating at 66 Hz

The i860 graphics accelerator and PixelStamp chipset provide
support for both normal and antialiased vectors and
Gouraud-shaded, Z-buffered models.  The Model 200PXG offers 3D
modeling and simple animation by supporting simultaneous
full-page double buffering and Z buffering.

U.S. List Price Configuration:
    o 16 Mbytes ECC memory (120 Mbytes maximum capacity)
    o 8 Plane acclerated 3D color frame buffer (24 planes
      maximum)
    o 19-inch Trinitron (tm) VRT19 color monitor
    o Diskless (Maximum disk capacity:  14 Gbytes)

List Price:  $29,100

DECstation 5000 Model 200PXG Turbo:

The DECstation 5000 Model 200PXG Turbo is designed for
high-performance 3D modeling and visualization applications.  In
addition to the same features as the Model 200PXG, the PXG Turbo
graphics option triple-width card features:
    o 24 Planes of high-resolution graphics with full-page double
