4-3 TURBOCHANNEL I/O INTERCONNECT FACT SHEET

   PRODUCT NAME:  TURBOchannel I/O Interconnect			
   								
   OVERVIEW:

   TURBOchannel I/O Interconnect is a new open, high-performance,
   low-cost I/O interconnect Digital is offering with its DECstation
   5000 Model 200 workstation family and DECsystem 5000 Model 200
   server, and will also be available on future DECstation
   workstations.  The TURBOchannel architecture defines a 32-bit,
   synchronous I/O channel that can operate at any fixed frequency in
   the range of 12.5 MHz to 25 MHz.  At the protocol level, it
   defines a maximum Direct Memory Access (DMA) burst transfer rate
   of 100 MBytes per second. The TURBOchannel implementation on the
   DECstation 5000 Model 200 operates at 25 MHz, and achieves DMA
   burst transfers of 93 MBytes per second.  Three TURBOchannel slots
   are available to users to enhance their base systems with a range
   of Digital-developed and third party options.

   KEY FEATURES:
       o Highest proven performance
       o Concise protocol results in simple interface
       o Highly integrated mechanical design, well-suited for
         desktop systems

COMPARISON CHART OF KEY BUS FEATURES:
