 Primary Board Area(sq. cm)    168       123      250      332      371	
 Maximum Physical Address       16GB	 256MB	    4GB	     4GB      4GB
 Licensable to option vendors  Yes       Yes       Yes     Yes      Yes
Licensable to system vendors   Yes       Yes   Restrictive Yes      Yes
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

   OPEN TURBOchannel LICENSING:

   The TURBOchannel Interconnect bus is available for license to all
   interested parties, including independent option and system
   vendors, on a no-charge, royalty-free basis.  The TURBOchannel
   architecture is an integral part of Digital's complete DECstation
   workstation open bus strategy, and builds on Digital's
   announcement of support for VMEbus and Futurebus+ made at
   BUSCON/90-WEST on February 14, 1990.

   Starting with the DECstation 5000 Model 200 workstation,  Digital
   offers users the flexibility of open I/O interconnects.  Through
   adapters, users will be able to connect VMEbus and, when
   available, Futurebus+ devices to the TURBOchannel Interconnect.

   TURBOchannel DEVELOPERS KIT:

   Comprehensive documentation will be made available to independent
   option and system vendors to assist them in developing products
   compatible with the TURBOchannel Interconnect.  The kit includes:

       	o TURBOchannel Hardware Specification
       	o TURBOchannel Option Mechanical Drawings
       	o ULTRIX Device Driver Guide
       	o TURBOchannel System Parameters

   The kit is currently undergoing human factors testing and will be
   available in June, 1990 for a $65 charge.  To begin an assessment
   of the TURBOchannel design, a TURBOchannel technical data sheet is
   available immediately by calling 1-800-678-OPEN.  It includes
   protocol description, timing diagrams, ROM overview, performance
   data, and an actual-size option mechanical drawing.  Other
   elements of the kit will be phased in as they become available,
   including:  the TURBOchannel Option and Systems Firmware
   Specification, a TURBOchannel Option Designers Guide,
   and a TURBOchannel System Designers Guide.

   Digital is also working with leading semiconductor manufacturers
   to make interface Application Specific Integrated Circuits (ASICs)
   and ASIC design services available to independent option vendors
   who are developing TURBOchannel options.

   TRI/ADD Program:

   Digital has created a new organization to provide technical and
   marketing support for independent hardware option and system
   vendors interested in developing options for TURBOchannel I/O
   Interconnect, VMEbus, and Small Computer System Interface (SCSI)
   interconnects.  The program will provide free technical consulting
   for independent vendors and will be fully activated in June 1990.
   For more information, all interested independent hardware option
