System Configurations:
Preconfigured DECsystem 5800 systems now include a choice of
in-cabinet RA90 storage (2.4 Gbytes) or in-cabinet RA70 storage
(560 Mbytes).  Up to eight RA70 5.25-inch disk drives (for a
total of 2.2 Gbytes) can be integrated into the CPU cabinet.

Systems can be configured with up to twelve KDB50 controllers,
supporting up to 58 Gbytes of local disk capacity (using RA90s).
The HSC70 is also supported by the DECsystem 5800 series,
providing a high throughput I/O connection to large numbers of
mass storage products and high-speed tapes.  DECsystem 5800
computers are available in 19" wide EIA-standard rack mountable
format.

Hardware and Software Configurations:
    o Entry-level DECsystem 5800 systems include:
      -	R3000 CPU (1 for DECsystem 5810, 2 for DECsystem 5820, 3
        for DECsystem 5830, and 4 for DECsystem 5840 computers)
      - Integral Floating Point
      -	32 MB ECC MOS Memory for DECsystem 5810; 64 Mbytes for
        DECsystem 5820, DECsystem 5830, and DECsystem 5840
        computers).
      -	12-slot VAXBI I/O Channel
      -	DEBNI (802.3 Ethernet Communications Interface)	
      -	TK70 Tape Drive & Interface
      -	KDB50 Disk Controller
      -	SA70 In-cabinet Storage Array (560 Mbytes)
      -	ULTRIX 2 User Base License
      -	ULTRIX 3-16 User License
      -	ULTRIX Workstation Software Server License
      -	1 Full Year Product Warranty

U.S. Pricing:
