Re: Problem: DECStation 3100 does not recognise extra 16MB of 3rd party memory.

SOLVED:
Thank you to all who replied to my problem of the 3rd party DECStation 3100
memory not being recognised. The problem turned out to be a bad SIMM, in fact
on close inspection, one of the logic ICs was cracked. It was unfortunate that
it was the first SIMM which was bad, or we may have spotted the problem
earlier. Some hints for the similarly afflicted:

* No you don't have to reconfigure the Kernel MEMSIZE option. According to DEC,
        this is used to size Kernel tables or somesuch.

* Run
        >>>t m
  For a complete memory test, instead of relying on system default tests.

Thank you all again,
