The DECstation 5000 has a security mode in the boot roms.  Although this
doesn't help with previous workstations, (and tackles the problem in a
different way) it is mentioned as a point of reference.

I believe the relevant console commands is "passwd" with the "-s" and
"-c" option.

If you specify

	>> passwd -s

You will be asked to specify a console password.  

	>> passwd -c

will clear the console password, and can only be invoked in "full"
console mode.

If the system is halted to console, or power-cycled, the prompt appears
as "S>" instead of ">>" and the only two commands that work are
"passwd", which asks for the password, and "boot".  The "-s" (single
user) flag on "boot" is not available.  So essentially all you can do is
boot (I haven't checked out all the other commands, such as
configuration checks).

One thing I haven't figured out yet is what you do if no one knows
either of the console or system passwords.  I suspect calling field
service is the only option...

