Don't be lulled into thinking this is secure. You can still ^C Ultrix when
it's booting and be dumped into single user mode.

>One thing I haven't figured out yet is what you do if no one knows
>either of the console or system passwords.  I suspect calling field
>service is the only option...
There is a pin on the system board which, when jumpered to ground, 
makes the system clear all nonvolatile RAM (where the password is
stored) on a system reset or powerup.  I believe this is discussed 
in some of the documentation.

