In article <408@latvax8.lat.oz>, CCHD@latvax8.lat.oz (Huw Davies - La Trobe University Computer Centre) writes:
> I have a VAXstation-2000 which I want to take interstate to run some
> tests with, but I don't want to take the monitor and keyboard (they
> won't fit in a plane!). Is there any way that I can get the system
> to boot without its monitor? I've tried setting various boot flags
> but to no avail.

VAXstations are 'smart': if they have a workstation interface card in the Qbus,
they will use that as the console. If you want an ordinary console, just remove
the interface card. It's not particularly hard to do. You must have a Grant
Continuity Card to put in the Qbus in its place (hope you're on good terms with
Field Circus).

